{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "CURATED INPUT. Candidate non-US-situs lines, seeded index-first rather than by crawling an issuer product list. Every candidate here is only a CANDIDATE -- scripts/build_ucits_universe.py validates each one against two independent sources (OpenFIGI for listing existence on the London exchange, Yahoo Finance for legal name / currency / TER / fund size) and DROPS anything that fails. Nothing enters data/ucits_universe.json unvalidated.",
    "why_not_scraped": "The iShares product list sits behind a terms-and-conditions acceptance gate, and no ungated source returns ISIN for London-listed lines. Rather than accept those terms or ship unverified domicile strings, the universe is seeded from the index side and validated. See structure_note for why this does not weaken the estate-tax verdict.",
    "structure_note": "UCITS is an EU framework: a fund cannot simultaneously be UCITS-authorised and US-domiciled. So UCITS status settles the estate-tax (situs) question structurally, without needing a per-line ISIN lookup. Fund domicile within the EU (Ireland vs Luxembourg) does NOT change the situs answer but DOES change US dividend withholding -- 15 per cent for Irish funds under the US-Ireland treaty, 30 per cent otherwise. These are tracked as two separate fields with separate confidence levels.",
    "etc_warning": "Entries marked structure=etc are exchange-traded COMMODITIES, not UCITS funds. They are debt securities issued by a special-purpose vehicle. Their situs treatment does not follow from UCITS status and must be resolved separately -- they are carried here but the builder marks their situs verdict as unresolved rather than safe.",
    "seeded": "2026-08-02",
    "fields": {
      "t": "London ticker, without the .L suffix Yahoo requires.",
      "idx": "Canonical index key, joins to data/index_map.json.",
      "iss": "Issuer, as a hint only -- the validated legal name from Yahoo overrides it.",
      "structure": "ucits_etf or etc.",
      "dist": "acc (accumulating) or dist (distributing). Load-bearing: comparing a distributing line against an accumulating line on PRICE returns produces a spurious drift exactly equal to the dividend yield."
    }
  },
  "curated_overrides": {
    "_note": "Fields Yahoo cannot supply, filled ONLY where a verified figure already exists in this repo or has been checked against the issuer. Yahoo returns no expense ratio for any Vanguard Ireland line -- a systematic gap, not a random one. The two figures below are carried over from the multi-source TER verification pass done for data/curated.json on 2026-07-09 (the pass that corrected five real errors). The remaining Vanguard lines are deliberately left blank rather than guessed: a wrong TER silently corrupts every cost comparison the tool makes. Fill them at the quarterly review against Vanguard's published KIID.",
    "VUAA": {"ter": 0.07, "ter_src": "curated.json 2026-07-09, >=2 issuer sources"},
    "VWRA": {"ter": 0.22, "ter_src": "curated.json 2026-07-09, >=2 issuer sources"}
  },
